<title>USA: NYSE Unavailables -.</title>
<headline>NYSE Unavailables -.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New York Stock Exchange said Thursday the Bank of New York and State Street Boston Corp were unavailable for after-hours trading due to news.</p>
<p>Bank of New York filed applications with the Federal Reserve Board and the Massachussetts Board of Bank Inc seeking approval to raise its stake in State Street Boston to 9.9 percent.</p>
<p>Corimon SACA, Westmoreland Coal Co and Westmoreland preferred A stock were also unavailable for trading.</p>
